# `dfo::PSPollPattern`

Which set of directions is polled.

`PositiveBasis2N` polls the `2n` points `±mesh` along each direction of a basis. `PositiveBasisNp1` polls the `n + 1` points of a minimal positive basis, which costs about half as many evaluations per poll but gives a coarser picture of the neighbourhood.

## Fields

### `PositiveBasis2N`

`enumerator`, default `0`.

The `2n` points `±mesh` along each basis direction.

### `PositiveBasisNp1`

`enumerator`, default `1`.

The `n + 1` points of a minimal positive basis.

## Guidance

Set as `PSConfig::poll_pattern`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

Evaluations per run.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  const auto rosenbrock = [](const Series &x) {
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0), b = x.select(0, 1);
    return (b - a * a).square() * 100.0 + (1.0 - a).square();
  };

  for (const auto pattern : {dfo::PSPollPattern::PositiveBasis2N, dfo::PSPollPattern::PositiveBasisNp1}) {
    dfo::PSConfig config;
    config.poll_pattern = pattern;
    config.search_strategy = dfo::PSSearchStrategy::Off;
    const dfo::PSOutcome o = dfo::pattern_search_minimizer(rosenbrock, pluss::series::make({-1.2, 1.0}), config);
    out.writeln(pattern == dfo::PSPollPattern::PositiveBasis2N ? "2N " : "N+1", ": evaluations =", o.diagnostics.evaluations, ", minimum =", o.minimum);
  }
}
```

### Example 2

In three variables the saving grows: `2n = 6` against `n + 1 = 4` points per poll.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - pluss::series::make({1.0, -1.0, 2.0})).square().sum(); };
  for (const auto pattern : {dfo::PSPollPattern::PositiveBasis2N, dfo::PSPollPattern::PositiveBasisNp1}) {
    dfo::PSConfig config;
    config.poll_pattern = pattern;
    const dfo::PSOutcome o = dfo::pattern_search_minimizer(f, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0, 0.0}), config);
    out.writeln(pattern == dfo::PSPollPattern::PositiveBasis2N ? "2N " : "N+1", ": evaluations =", o.diagnostics.evaluations);
  }
}
```

### Example 3

Both reach the same answer on a smooth problem.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  dfo::PSConfig config;
  config.poll_pattern = dfo::PSPollPattern::PositiveBasisNp1;
  out.writeln("N+1 minimizer =", dfo::pattern_search_minimizer(f, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), config).minimizer.items<double>());
}
```

